"title": "Nazareth",
"media_type": "Text",
"index_reference": "nazareth",
"language": "eng",
"review_level": "None",
"content": "<p><b>Nazareth</b> is a small town in the region of <a href=\"#t55\">Galilee</a>, in the north of <a href=\"#t74\">Israel</a>. Nazareth does not appear in the Old Testament, and the first time we hear about this town is when we hear that <a href=\"#t89\">Mary</a> and Joseph, Jesus's parents, came from Nazareth. Jesus was born in a village called <a href=\"#t13\">Bethlehem</a>, in <a href=\"#t81\">Judea</a>, but when he was still small Mary and Joseph went to live in Nazareth. Therefore Jesus was later called a Nazarene, which means someone from Nazareth. That was not a compliment. The <a href=\"#t77\">Jews</a> from Judea looked down on the people in Galilee, and even the people within Galilee looked down on people from Nazareth, because it was a small and unimportant town.</p>",
